cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "SmashTable: Safer Transactional Associative In-Memory Collection Types with Vectorization"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
license: Apache-2.0
version: 1.0.0-rc.1
repository-code: https://github.com/ashvardanian/SmashTable
url: https://github.com/ashvardanian/SmashTable
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.22030408
abstract: >-
  SmashTable makes one update span several containers safely: either every change lands or none
  does, whether a competing writer or an exception interrupts it, and a commit spanning two or more
  containers asks each for permission before the first one writes. Every store declares its
  isolation level at compile time, the tests check that level against behaviour, and the commit
  protocols are verified as Promela models and GenMC clients. Cores range from vectors, AVL,
  weight-balanced and hash trees to immutable B-trees, S+ trees and Elias-Fano sets that search a
  whole row per vectorized pass, and a pinned atomic hash table that also runs on GPUs, shipped as
  header-only templates with Python and Rust bindings.

authors:
